	(text "====================================================================\nILI9341 40-PIN DISPLAY TO ESP32-S3 WROOM-1 WIRING LOG (4-WIRE SPI)\n====================================================================\n\n[POWER & GROUND]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDisplay Pin 5 (GND)       --> Connect to GND\nDisplay Pin 6 (IOVCC)     --> Connect to 3.3V Power Rail\nDisplay Pin 16 (GND)      --> Connect to GND\nDisplay Pin 37 (GND)      --> Connect to GND\n\n[SPI DATA & CONTROL LINES]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDisplay Pin 7 (RESET)     --> Connect to ESP32 Pin 5 (RST)\nDisplay Pin 9 (CS)        --> Connect to ESP32 Pin 18 (CS)\nDisplay Pin 10 (SCL/SCK)  --> Connect to ESP32 Pin 20 (SCK)\nDisplay Pin 11 (WR/A0)    --> Connect to 3.3V Power Rail\nDisplay Pin 12 (RD)       --> Connect to 3.3V Power Rail\nDisplay Pin 13 (SDI/SDA)  --> Connect to ESP32 Pin 21 (MOSI)\nDisplay Pin 14 (SDO)      --> Connect to ESP32 Pin 22 (MISO) [Optional]\nDisplay Pin 15 (RESET)    --> Connect to ESP32 Pin 5 (RST) [Duplicate Line]\n*Note: Connect ESP32 Pin 4 (DC) to your design's dedicated Data/Command control line if required by your display's specific 4-wire hardware mapping.\n\n[INTERFACE MODE SELECTION (SPI MODE CONFIG)]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDisplay Pin 38 (IM0)      --> Connect to 3.3V Power Rail (Logic 1)\nDisplay Pin 39 (IM1)      --> Connect to GND (Logic 0)\nDisplay Pin 40 (IM2)      --> Connect to 3.3V Power Rail (Logic 1)\n\n[UNUSED DATA BUS PINS - MUST BE GROUNDED FOR SPI]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDisplay Pins 17 thru 24 (DB0 to DB7)   --> Connect ALL to GND\nDisplay Pins 25 thru 32 (DB8 to DB15)  --> Connect ALL to GND\n\n[BACKLIGHT POWER]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDisplay Pin 33 (LED-A)    --> Connect to 3.3V Power Rail via a 10-47 Ohm resistor\nDisplay Pin 34 (LED-K1)   --> Connect to GND\nDisplay Pin 35 (LED-K2)   --> Connect to GND\nDisplay Pin 36 (LED-K3)   --> Connect to GND\n\n[NOT CONNECTED / LEAVE OPEN]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nDisplay Pin 1 (XL)        --> Leave Disconnected (No Touch)\nDisplay Pin 2 (YU)        --> Leave Disconnected (No Touch)\nDisplay Pin 3 (XR)        --> Leave Disconnected (No Touch)\nDisplay Pin 4 (YD)        --> Leave Disconnected (No Touch)\nDisplay Pin 8 (FMARK)     --> Leave Disconnected\n====================================================================\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
